Conformance
Id	Clause
conformance.1	This module specification describes the module that supplies the schema of what a model is given and generates in the Anthropic Messages API [ANTHROPIC-API], as the beta types of the Anthropic Python SDK write it [ANTHROPIC-SDK], to the module that reads a recording of it. It is a module specification of the living-memory specification, and restates nothing that specification states.
conformance.2	The key words "MUST", "MUST NOT", "REQUIRED", "SHALL", "SHALL NOT", "SHOULD", "SHOULD NOT", "RECOMMENDED", "NOT RECOMMENDED", "MAY", and "OPTIONAL" in this specification are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 [BCP14] when, and only when, they appear in all capitals, as shown here.
conformance.3	The Rules are normative. A rule's Id names what it governs: kept, what the module supplies; schema, how the schema is derived. This specification has no optional features.
Rules
Id	Rule
kept.1	The model is given the prior conversational turns as input messages and generates the next message; the system prompt gives it context and instructions; tools are the tools it may use [ANTHROPIC-API]. The module MUST supply the schema of these parts only: a request's system, tools and messages, and a response's content; the request's other members and the response's other members are not kept.
schema.1	A beta request adds members to the request and content blocks to its messages, among them tool_addition [ANTHROPIC-SDK]. The schema MUST be derived type by type from the SDK's beta types, for the kept parts only: the beta request's system, tools and messages, and the beta response's content, into a JSON Schema of draft-07 [JSON-SCHEMA-07].
schema.2	The SDK writes each type as a Python class or alias [PEP484]. A TypedDict, written as a class or by its alternative syntax [PEP589], MUST be an object whose required keys are those marked Required, or all of them where it is total [PEP655]; a BaseModel MUST be an object whose required fields are those without a default; Union MUST be anyOf, Optional anyOf with null, Literal an enum [PEP586], Iterable, List and Sequence an array of their items, Dict[str, X] an object of X, and object any value. An alternative no JSON text can hold, a file or a path the SDK reads before sending, MUST be left out, a JSON value being only false, null, true, an object, an array, a number or a string [RFC8259]. A definition read under if TYPE_CHECKING is the one a type checker reads [PEP484].
schema.3	Each named type MUST be a definition reached by $ref [JSON-SCHEMA-07], named by its type's name where its package exports it, else by its module's name, '.', and its name, and MUST cite the file that defines it. Each object MUST be left open, so a member newer than the SDK's commit is kept, as omitting additionalProperties allows every member [JSON-SCHEMA-07].
schema.4	The schema is a generated file: it MUST be generated from the SDK's type files by the generator the implementation holds, MUST say at its start that it is generated, and MUST ship with the type files it is generated from and their licence [ANTHROPIC-SDK].
